e POINT \\((h, k)\\) is the center of the translated graph. For \\(g(x)\\), center is \\((3, 2)\\).''\\\\\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:225:\\begin{callout}{\\IconBook\\ TRANSLATED RECIPROCAL --- \\(g(x) = 1/(x-h) + k\\)}{calloutyellow}\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:230:\\textbullet\\ Example: \\(g(x) = 1/(x-3) + 2\\) \\(\\rightarrow\\) asymptotes \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 2\\).\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:234:\\hspace*{1.5em}\\textbullet\\ y-intercept: set \\(x = 0\\). \\(y = 1/(0-h) + k = -1/h + k.\\)\\\\\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:235:\\hspace*{1.5em}\\textbullet\\ x-intercept: set \\(y = 0\\). Solve \\(0 = 1/(x-h) + k \\rightarrow x = h - 1/k.\\)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:244:  \\item Laps 1-3: Try-It 4 + \\#11 + \\#18. Parent-form scaled/reflected. (5-6 min each.)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:245:  \\item Laps 4-5: Try-It 5 + \\#19 --- translated forms. \\#19 is the assessment rehearsal --- press on BOTH asymptotes AND intercepts.\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:251:  \\item 6 items in order. Parent forms first (Try-It 4, \\#11, \\#18), then translations (Try-It 5, \\#19, \\#21).\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:252:  \\item For \\#19: BEFORE graphing, state \\((h, k)\\), asymptotes, and domain/range.\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:261:  \\item For \\#19: what are the asymptotes? What are the intercepts?\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:263:}{Solo teacher: 6 laps. Press BOTH asymptotes AND intercepts on \\#19. This IS the assessment rehearsal.}\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:267:  \\item Try It 4 --- Graph \\(g(x) = 10/x\\) (scaled parent)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:268:  \\item Practice \\#11 --- Error Analysis: \\(y = 5/x\\)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:269:  \\item Practice \\#18 --- Graph \\(y = -2/x\\) (reflected parent)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:270:  \\item Try It 5 --- Graph \\(g(x) = 1/(x+2) - 4\\) (translated)\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:271:  \\item Practice \\#19 \\IconStar\\ ASSESSMENT CRITICAL --- \\(g(x) = 1/(x-2) + 6\\) + intercepts\ntex/L41_P3_teacher.tex:272:  \\item Practice \\#21 --- Video game storage (modeled)\ntex/L41_P