 in `questionbank/registry.jsonl`. No fabricated items. If the right Savvas item isn't in the bank, ingest it first (screenshots live in `questionbank/images/`).\n   9: - **Single-DOK3 spine, per period.** One DOK-3 driver per period, self-contained with all rules printed on the page. A lesson's P3 may have no DOK-3 driver (pure DOK-2 mastery day) when P2 already carried the spine. See wiki `concepts/Single-DOK3 Lesson Spine.md`.\n  10: - **Summary exit, not CER.** Walk-out tasks recap the day's learning with fill-in + one \"biggest thing learned\" sentence. Full CER writing in 5 min is unrealistic.\n  11: - **Blooket is DEPRECATED** for all lessons from Unit 4 onward. Do Now now carries DOK-1 recall load. Existing Blooket CSVs moved to `legacy/`.\n  12: - **Try-Its stay in-class as Think-Pair-Share.** Student homework completion is unreliable. The Lynn DOK framework wants 35\u00e2\u20ac\u201c40 min of student heavy lifting in Explore \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Try-Its fill that. Back-of-packet HW is OPTIONAL REINFORCEMENT only.\n  13: - **Klimsara-adapted 3-period cadence** (default going forward). Each lesson = 3 teaching periods. Teacher models ONE Example in Launch; Explore is the 35-min TPS block; student-centered, not teacher-modeled-end-to-end.\n  14: - **Framework phases** (non-negotiable, per `DOKframework.txt`): Do Now (\u00e2\u2030\u00a410) \u00c2\u00b7 Launch (10\u00e2\u20ac\u201c15) \u00c2\u00b7 Explore (35\u00e2\u20ac\u201c40) \u00c2\u00b7 Share/Summary (5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c15) \u00c2\u00b7 Exit Ticket. Teacher packet carries explicit `Questions to ask:` and `Adult role:` per phase for evaluators.\n  15: \n  16: ## Current structure \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Klimsara-adapted (Unit 4+)\n  17: \n  18: Each lesson picks ONE cadence:\n  19: \n  20: - **Full 3-period** = `L{NN}_P1_*` + `L{NN}_P2_*` + `L{NN}_P3_*`. Pacer has three sub-tabs.\n  21: - **Single-period quick** = `L{NN}_P1_*` only. Condensed Klimsara, DOK-3 spine inside the one period. Functionally complete \u00e2\u20ac\u201d NOT a stub awaiting P2/P3. File naming keeps `_P1_` for builder-output consistency.\n  22: \n  23: To tell which cadence a lesson uses, read the builder docstring (`build_L{NN}_P1_packets.py` line 1\u00e2\u20ac\u201c24). Assessment-day shells follow `L{topic_close+1}_*` (e.g. `L35_P4_*`, `L46_*`).\n  24: \n  25: The three-period template below describes the full cadence:\n  26: \n  27: | Period | Role | DOK arc | Typical Explore load |\n  28: |---|---|---|---|\n  29: | **P1** | Conceptual introduction | 1 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 2 | Do Now (bridge) + 2 Examples modeled + 5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c7 Practice/Try-It items in TPS |\n  30: | **P2** | Applications + DOK-3 spine | 2 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 3 | Bridge + 1 Example modeled + 4 Practice + **\u00e2\u00ad\u0090 DOK-3 driver** |\n  31: | **P3** | Mastery / assessment-critical | 2 | Bridge + 2 Examples paired in Launch + 5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c6 Practice (assessment-aligned) |\n  32: \n  33: **Wednesday F 45-min variant**: Explore cut to 25 min (drop 2 practice items), Launch/Share/Exit unchanged. Framework phases never cut.\n  34: \n  35: ### Lesson 3-5 (closed)\n  36: \n  37: Originally 8 days. Retired to `legacy/`. Replaced by Klimsara close-out:\n  38: \n  39: | Period | File prefix | DOK-3 driver | Content |\n  40: |---|---|---|---|\n  41: | P2 (Tue 4/28) | `L35_P2_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Multiplicity + factored-form graphing |\n  42: | P3 (Wed 4/29) | `L35_P3_*` | **Practice #27 (Storage Box)** | Real+complex zeros + modeling |\n  43: | P4 (Thu 4/30) | `L35_P4_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Topic 3 Assessment (11 Qs, external `a2topic3assess.docx`) |\n  44: \n  45: ### Lesson 4-1 (ready, Fri F / Mon A start)\n  46: \n  47: | Period | File prefix | DOK-3 driver | Content |\n  48: |---|---|---|---|\n  49: | P1 | `L41_P1_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Inverse variation introduction (xy = k, y = k/x) |\n  50: | P2 | `L41_P2_*` | **Practice #26 (Ram\u00c3\u00b3n road trip \u00e2\u20ac\u201d direct-vs-inverse)** | Applications + DOK-3 performance task |\n  51: | P3 | `L41_P3_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Reciprocal function + translations (**assessment-critical**: Topic 4 LEHS Q#3 + Q#5) |\n  52: \n  53: ## Naming conventions\n  54: \n  55: - **Artifacts:** `L{NN}_P{N}_{Do_Now,Student_Packet,Teacher_Packet,Slides,Visuals_Checklist}.{docx,pptx,md}`. Replaces legacy `Day_N_*`.\n  56: - **Bank IDs:** `{lesson}-savvas-q{N}` for practice items (e.g. `4-1-savvas-q26`); longer auto-slugs for Examples/Try-Its/TE addendums.\n  57: \n  58: ## Standard toolchain\n  59: \n  60: **Canonical output path (LaTeX):**\n  61: - `tex/preamble.sty` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d shared LaTeX style package (tcolorbox callouts, framework_phase_header, sentence_frame_box, summary_exit_box, bank_item, day_banner, section_banner; ASCII emoji macros for portability).\n  62: - `tex/L{NN}_P{N}_{student,teacher}.tex` + `.pdf` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d per-lesson packets. Edits go here directly. Regenerate PDF with `pdflatex --miktex-enable-installer L{NN}_P{N}_{student,teacher}.tex`.\n  63: \n  64: **Content source & intent tooling:**\n  65: - `qb.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d registry accessor. `qb.get_for_packet(ids)` used by both LaTeX prompts (read-only) and retired docx builders.\n  66: - `qb_append.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d validates + appends registry entries. Required fields: `lesson`, `prompt`, `dok`. Optional schema includes `visual_type` (enum: `none`/`photo`/`graph`/`table`/`diagram`/`map`), `visual_needs_cleanup` (bool), `visual_clean_asset` (path).\n  67: - `generate_practice_skeletons.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d given a lesson's calibration file, emits pre-filled JSON stubs for every Savvas practice item.\n  68: - `fix_registry_mojibake.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ftfy-based registry encoding cleanup (e.g. `\u00c3\u0192\u00e2\u20ac\u0161\u00c3\u201a\u00c2\u00b0` \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `\u00c2\u00b0`).\n  69: - `extract_intent_anchors.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d walks `build_L*_packets.py` via AST and emits `graph/eye_check/L{NN}_P{N}.md` briefs of every