esson slide decks. Not yet migrated to LaTeX; stays as-is pending demand.\n  86: \n  87: **Archive:**\n  88: - `legacy/` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d retired Day 2-8 artifacts, Blooket CSVs, and (as of 2026-04-22) the docx packet outputs + Visuals Checklists.\n  89: \n  90: ## Class context (as of 2026-04-20)\n  91: \n  92: - Two sections: **Period A** and **Period F**.\n  93: - **Week of 2026-04-27 schedule** (saved in project memory): Mon A 65 / Tue F 65 + A 55 / Wed A 65 + F **45** / Thu F 65 + A 55 / Fri F 65.\n  94: - **Period A** is one period behind Period F at start of 3-5 close-out. Both finish Topic 3 Thu 4/30. Period F starts 4-1 on Fri 5/1; Period A starts 4-1 on Mon 5/4.\n  95: - **Wednesday F = 45 min** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d short variant with Explore cut.\n  96: - **Solo teacher, class \u00e2\u2030\u00a410.** No aide-based release valves. Single-teacher circulation (4\u00e2\u20ac\u201c6 laps during Explore).\n  97: - **ELL-heavy** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d sentence frames on student packet are non-negotiable.\n  98: \n  99: ## Assessment coverage\n 100: \n 101: - **Topic 3 assessment (Thu 4/30)** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `a2topic3assess.docx`. 11 Qs spanning 3-1 through 3-5. Of these, 4 are Lesson 3-5 content: Q#2 (conjugate pairs \u00e2\u20ac\u201d preped via Tue\u00e2\u2020\u2019Wed bridge prompt), Q#5 (zeros + end behavior), Q#6 (Lucy's tray volume model \u00e2\u20ac\u201d paralleled by Storage Box #27 on Wed), Q#10 (identify zeros).\n 102: - **Topic 4 LEHS 8-Q assessment** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `a2topic4assess.docx`, 8 selected items: #2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7, #15, #19. Of these, 2 are Lesson 4-1 content: Q#3 (H/V asymptotes, from Ex 4/5), Q#5 (translation description, from Ex 5). **Practice #19 is the rehearsal item** for these.\n 103: \n 104: ## Related wiki pages (obsidian-wiki, home laptop)\n 105: \n 106: - `concepts/Klimsara-Adapted Lesson Pattern.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 3-period template, phase timings, TPS rule, Wed-F variant\n 107: - `concepts/Single-DOK3 Lesson Spine.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d updated: per-period, not per-lesson\n 108: - `concepts/Self-Contained Pacer Pattern.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d v3 tabbed pattern\n 109: - `concepts/Do Now A-B-C Framework.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the school's Do Now sub-phasing convention\n 110: \n 111: ---\n 112: \n 113: <!-- gitnexus:start -->\n 114: # GitNexus \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Code Intelligence\n 115: \n 116: This project is indexed by GitNexus as **Lesson_planning** (29 symbols, 71 relationships, 6 execution flows). Use the GitNexus MCP tools to understand code, assess impact, and navigate safely.\n 117: \n 118: > If any GitNexus tool warns the index is stale, run `npx gitnexus analyze` in terminal first.\n 119: \n 120: ## Always Do\n 121: \n 122: - **MUST run impact analysis before editing any symbol.** Before modifying a function, class, or method, run `gitnexus_impact({target: \"symbolName\", direction: \"upstream\"})` and report the blast radius (direct callers, affected processes, risk level) to the user.\n 123: - **MUST run `gitnexus_detect_changes()` before committing** to verify your changes only affect expected symbols and execution flows.\n 124: - **MUST warn the user** if impact analysis returns HIGH or CRITICAL risk before proceeding with edits.\n 125: - When exploring unfamiliar code, use `gitnexus_query({query: \"concept\"})` to find execution flows instead of grepping. It returns process-grouped results ranked by relevance.\n 126: - When you need full context on a specific symbol \u00e2\u20ac\u201d callers, callees, which execution flows it participates in \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use `gitnexus_context({name: \"symbolName\"})`.\n 127: \n 128: ## When Debugging\n 129: \n 130: 1. `gitnexus_query({query: \"<error or symptom>\"})` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d find execution flows related to the issue\n 131: 2. `gitnexus_context({name: \"<suspect function>\"})` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d see all callers, callees, and process participation\n 132: 3. `READ gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/process/{processName}` 