: \"MATCH ...\"})` |\n 158: \n 159: ## Impact Risk Levels\n 160: \n 161: | Depth | Meaning | Action |\n 162: |-------|---------|--------|\n 163: | d=1 | WILL BREAK \u00e2\u20ac\u201d direct callers/importers | MUST update these |\n 164: | d=2 | LIKELY AFFECTED \u00e2\u20ac\u201d indirect deps | Should test |\n 165: | d=3 | MAY NEED TESTING \u00e2\u20ac\u201d transitive | Test if critical path |\n 166: \n 167: ## Resources\n 168: \n 169: | Resource | Use for |\n 170: |----------|---------|\n 171: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/context` | Codebase overview, check index freshness |\n 172: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/clusters` | All functional areas |\n 173: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/processes` | All execution flows |\n 174: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/process/{name}` | Step-by-step execution trace |\n 175: \n 176: ## Self-Check Before Finishing\n 177: \n 178: Before completing any code modification task, verify:\n 179: 1. `gitnexus_impact` was run for all modified symbols\n 180: 2. No HIGH/CRITICAL risk warnings were ignored\n 181: 3. `gitnexus_detect_changes()` confirms changes match expected scope\n 182: 4. All d=1 (WILL BREAK) dependents were updated\n 183: \n 184: ## Keeping the Index Fresh\n 185: \n 186: After committing code changes, the GitNexus index becomes stale. Re-run analyze to update it:\n 187: \n 188: ```bash\n 189: npx gitnexus analyze\n 190: ```\n 191: \n 192: If the index previously included embeddings, preserve them by adding `--embeddings`:\n 193: \n 194: ```bash\n 195: npx gitnexus analyze --embeddings\n 196: ```\n 197: \n 198: To check whether embeddings exist, inspect `.gitnexus/meta.json` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the `stats.embeddings` field shows the count (0 means no embeddings). **Running analyze without `--embeddings` will delete any previously generated embeddings.**\n 199: \n 200: > Claude Code users: A PostToolUse hook handles this automatically after `git commit` and `git merge`.\n 201: \n 202: ## CLI\n 203: \n 204: 