PPORT FOR IEP STUDENTS}{calloutiep}\n 430: \\textbullet\\ Provide both Rule cards as half-sheet cut-outs on their desks.\\\\\n 431: \\textbullet\\ For \\#19, provide a pre-axed grid (labeled \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) from -4 to 8) so they don't spend time drawing axes.\\\\\n 432: \\textbullet\\ Accept verbal asymptote identification in lieu of written.\n 433: \\end{callout}\n 434: \n 435: \\begin{callout}{\\IconGlobe\\ SUPPORTS FOR ELL STUDENTS}{calloutell}\n 436: \\textbullet\\ Sentence frames on student page (don't skip).\\\\\n 437: \\textbullet\\ Word cards: ``asymptote'' = line the graph approaches but never touches.\\\\\n 438: \\textbullet\\ ``reciprocal'' = the fraction flipped; \\(1/x\\) is the reciprocal of \\(x\\).\\\\\n 439: \\textbullet\\ ``translation'' = shift of the whole graph (no rotation or resize).\\\\\n 440: \\textbullet\\ Pair ELL students with English-dominant partners for TPS.\n 441: \\end{callout}\n 442: \n 443: \\end{document}\n\ncodex\nI have the core files loaded. Next I\u2019m narrowing to the slide frames and the matching student/teacher packet sections so I can check answer leakage, item fidelity, phase timing, and style drift against the P2 deck.\nexec\n\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$targets = @(\n  @{file='\"'tex/L41_P3_slides.tex'; start=1; end=140},\n  @{file='tex/L41_P2_slides.tex'; start=1; end=130},\n  @{file='tex/L41_P3_student.tex'; start=120; end=240},\n  @{file='tex/L41_P3_teacher.tex'; start=145; end=380}\n);\nforeach (\"'$t in $targets) {\n  Write-Output \"===== $($t.file):$($t.start)-$($t.end) =====\";\n  $lines = Get-Content $t.file;\n  for ($i=$t.start; $i -le [Math]::Min($t.end, $lines.Length); $i++) {\n    '\"'{0,4}: {1}' -f \"'$i, $lines[$i-1]\n  }\n}' in C:\\Users\\rober\\Downloads\\Projects\\Lesson_planning\nexec\n\"C:\\\\Windows\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command \"rg -n \\\"Practice \\\\\\\\#13|Try It 4|Practice \\\\\\\\#11|Practi