ace{0.2cm}\n  99: \\begin{projcard}{Complete on your exit ticket}{slidegold}\n 100: \\begin{enumerate}\n 101:   \\setlength{\\itemsep}{0.2cm}\n 102:   \\item Today I learned that \\underline{\\hspace{5cm}}.\n 103:   \\item The biggest trap in Ram\u00c3\u00b3n's task was \\underline{\\hspace{5cm}}.\n 104:   \\item I distinguish direct from inverse variation by \\underline{\\hspace{5cm}}.\n 105: \\end{enumerate}\n 106: \\end{projcard}\n 107: \\end{frame}\n 108: \n 109: \\end{document}\n\n succeeded in 880ms:\n   1: # Lesson_planning \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Project Guidance\n   2: \n   3: High school Algebra 2 lesson materials \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Topic 3 (Polynomials) closing, Topic 4 (Rational Functions + Inverse Variation) beginning, then selected 5-x / trig / 6-x through end of school year (2026-06-20).\n   4: \n   5: ## Hard rules\n   6: \n   7: - **LaTeX is canonical for student-facing output** (as of 2026-04-22). The `tex/L{NN}_P{N}_{student,teacher}.pdf` files are what prints and what students/evaluators see. docx outputs are retired to `legacy/docx/` for reference. Python builders (`build_L*_packets.py`) remain as the structural intent source and drive the eye-check / polish worksheet tooling, but their docx outputs are no longer shipped. Edits to student-facing content go into `tex/*.tex` directly; regenerate PDF with `pdflatex --miktex-enable-installer`.\n   8: - **Savvas-only for student-facing work.** Every problem, Try It, Do Now, Practice, or Exit item on a student packet MUST trace to a Savvas bank ID in `questionbank/registry.jsonl`. No fabricated items. If the right Savvas item isn't in the bank, ingest it first (screenshots live in `questionbank/images/`).\n   9: - **Single-DOK3 spine, per period.** One DOK-3 driver per period, self-contained with all rules printed on the page. A lesson's P3 may have no DOK-3 driver (pure DOK-2 mastery day) when P2 already carried the spine. See wiki `concepts/Single-DOK3 Lesson Spine.md`.\n  10: - **Summary exit, not CER.** Walk-out tasks recap the day's learning with fill-in + one \"biggest thing learned\" sentence. Full CER writing in 5 min is unrealistic.\n  11: - **Blooket is DEPRECATED** for all lessons from Unit 4 onward. Do Now now carries DOK-1 recall load. Existing Blooket CSVs moved to `legacy/`.\n  12: - **Try-Its stay in-class as Think-Pair-Share.** Student homework completion is unreliable. The Lynn DOK framework wants 35\u00e2\u20ac\u201c40 min of student heavy lifting in Explore \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Try-Its fill that. Back-of-packet HW is OPTIONAL REINFORCEMENT only.\n  13: - **Klimsara-adapted 3-period cadence** (default going forward). Each lesson = 3 teaching periods. Teacher models ONE Example in Launch; Explore is the 35-min TPS block; student-centered, not teacher-modeled-end-to-end.\n  14: - **Framework phases** (non-negotiable, per `DOKframework.txt`): Do Now (\u00e2\u2030\u00a410) \u00c2\u00b7 Launch (10\u00e2\u20ac\u201c15) \u00c2\u00b7 Explore (35\u00e2\u20ac\u201c40) \u00c2\u00b7 Share/Summary (5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c15) \u00c2\u00b7 Exit Ticket. Teacher packet carries explicit `Questions to ask:` and `Adult role:` per phase for evaluators.\n  15: \n  16: ## Current structure \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Klimsara-adapted (Unit 4+)\n  17: \n  18: Each lesson picks ONE cadence:\n  19: \n  20: - **Full 3-period** = `L{NN}_P1_*` + `L{NN}_P2_*` + `L{NN}_P3_*`. Pacer has three sub-tabs.\n  21: - **Single-period quick** = `L{NN}_P1_*` only. Condensed Klimsara, DOK-3 spine inside the one period. Functionally complete \u00e2\u20ac\u201d NOT a stub awaiting P2/P3. File naming keeps `_P1_` for builder-output consistency.\n  22: \n  23: To tell which cadence a lesson uses, read the builder docstring (`build_L{NN}_P1_packets.py` line 1\u00e2\u20ac\u201c24). Assessment-day shells follow `L{topic_close+1}_*` (e.g. `L35_P4_*`, `L46_*`).\n  24: \n  25: The three-period template below describes the full cadence:\n  26: \n  27: | Period | Role | DOK arc | Typical Explore load |\n  28: |---|---|---|---|\n  29: | **P1** | Conceptual introduction | 1 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 2 | Do Now (bridge) + 2 Examples modeled + 5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c7 Practice/Try-It items in TPS |\n  30: | **P2** | Applications + DOK-3 spine | 2 \u00e2\u2020\u2019 3 | Bridge + 1 Example modeled + 4 Practice + **\u00e2\u00ad\u0090 DOK-3 driver** |\n  31: | **P3** | Mastery / assessment-critical | 2 | Bridge + 2 Examples paired in Launch + 5\u00e2\u20ac\u201c6 Practice (assessment-aligned) |\n  32: \n  33: **Wednesday F 45-min variant**: Explore cut to 25 min (drop 2 practice items), Launch/Share/Exit unchanged. Framework phases never cut.\n  34: \n  35: ### Lesson 3-5 (closed)\n  36: \n  37: Originally 8 days. Retired to `legacy/`. Replaced by Klimsara close-out:\n  38: \n  39: | Period | File prefix | DOK-3 driver | Content |\n  40: |---|---|---|---|\n  41: | P2 (Tue 4/28) | `L35_P2_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Multiplicity + factored-form graphing |\n  42: | P3 (Wed 4/29) | `L35_P3_*` | **Practice #27 (Storage Box)** | Real+complex zeros + modeling |\n  43: | P4 (Thu 4/30) | `L35_P4_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Topic 3 Assessment (11 Qs, external `a2topic3assess.docx`) |\n  44: \n  45: ### Lesson 4-1 (ready, Fri F / Mon A start)\n  46: \n  47: | Period | File prefix | DOK-3 driver | Content |\n  48: |---|---|---|---|\n  49: | P1 | `L41_P1_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Inverse variation introduction (xy = k, y = k/x) |\n  50: | P2 | `L41_P2_*` | **Practice #26 (Ram\u00c3\u00b3n road trip \u00e2\u20ac\u201d direct-vs-inverse)** | Applications + DOK-3 performance task |\n  51: | P3 | `L41_P3_*` | \u00e2\u20ac\u201d | Reciprocal function + translations (**assessment-critical**: Topic 4 LEHS Q#3 + Q#5) |\n  52: \n  53: ## Naming conventions\n  54: \n  55: - **Artifacts:** `L{NN}_P{N}_{Do_Now,Student_Packet,Teacher_Packet,Slides,Visuals_Checklist}.{docx,pptx,md}`. Replaces legacy `Day_N_*`.\n  56: - **Bank IDs:** `{lesson}-savvas-q{N}` for practice items (e.g. `4-1-savvas-q26`); longer auto-slugs for Examples/Try-Its/TE addendums.\n  57: \n  58: ## Standard toolchain\n  59: \n  60: **Canonical output path (LaTeX):**\n  61: - `tex/preamble.sty` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d shared LaTeX style package (tcolorbox callouts, framework_phase_header, sentence_frame_box, summary_exit_box, bank_item, day_banner, section_banner; ASCII emoji macros for portability).\n  62: - `tex/L{NN}_P{N}_{student,teacher}.tex` + `.pdf` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d per-lesson packets. Edits go here directly. Regenerate PDF with `pdflatex --miktex-enable-installer L{NN}_P{N}_{student,teacher}.tex`.\n  63: \n  64: **Content source & intent tooling:**\n  65: - `qb.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d registry accessor. `qb.get_for_packet(ids)` used by both LaTeX prompts (read-only) and retired docx builders.\n  66: - `qb_append.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d validates + appends registry entries. Required fields: `lesson`, `prompt`, `dok`. Optional schema includes `visual_type` (enum: `none`/`photo`/`graph`/`table`/`diagram`/`map`), `visual_needs_cleanup` (bool), `visual_clean_asset` (path).\n  67: - `generate_practice_skeletons.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d given a lesson's calibration file, emits pre-filled JSON stubs for every Savvas practice item.\n  68: - `fix_registry_mojibake.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d ftfy-based registry encoding cleanup (e.g. `\u00c3\u0192\u00e2\u20ac\u0161\u00c3\u201a\u00c2\u00b0` \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `\u00c2\u00b0`).\n  69: - `extract_intent_anchors.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d walks `build_L*_packets.py` via AST and emits `graph/eye_check/L{NN}_P{N}.md` briefs of every callout, phase header, bank item in source order. Used as the spec for LaTeX dispatches.\n  70: - `qb_polish_worksheet.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d per-builder polish worksheets in `graph/polish/` with prereq/rehearses-aware redundancy filter.\n  71: - `qb_diagnose.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d emits `graph/{skill_bridge_gaps,nominal_rehearsals,redundant_practice}.md`.\n  72: \n  73: **Retired (moved to `legacy/py/` 2026-04-22):**\n  74: - `legacy/py/build_L*_packets.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d original docx emitters (18 lessons). Frozen. Not re-run; any structural edits go into `tex/*.tex` or `lessons/*.yaml` instead.\n  75: - `legacy/py/packet_styles.py`, `legacy/py/packet_build.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d docx primitives called only by the retired builders.\n  76: - `legacy/py/refactor_builders_to_packet_build.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d historical one-shot refactor utility.\n  77: - `legacy/py/extract_intent_anchors.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d AST-walks the retired builders \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `graph/eye_check/*.md` briefs. The briefs are already committed and were consumed as inputs to the LaTeX-dispatch pass; not regenerated going forward.\n  78: - `legacy/py/tagging/extract_operational_ids.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d AST-walks the retired builders \u00e2\u2020\u2019 `tagging/operational_ids.json`. The JSON is already committed and is the snapshot `qb_polish_worksheet.py` reads against.\n  79: - `backfill_visuals_4-1.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d historical one-off, kept at repo root.\n  80: \n  81: Polish worksheets (`qb_polish_worksheet.py`) still runnable: they read the frozen `tagging/operational_ids.json`, not the Python builders. Useful if the questionbank registry changes.\n  82: \n  83: **Operational:**\n  84: - `L{35,41}_Pacer.html` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d single-file pacer per lesson, 3 sub-tabs per period, countdown timer, inline teacher scripts / answer keys / rules / bridges. Used live in the classroom \u00e2\u20ac\u201d NOT deprecated.\n  85: - `build_L{35,41}_slides.py` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d per-lesson slide decks. Not yet migrated to LaTeX; stays as-is pending demand.\n  86: \n  87: **Archive:**\n  88: - `legacy/` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d retired Day 2-8 artifacts, Blooket CSVs, and (as of 2026-04-22) the docx packet outputs + Visuals Checklists.\n  89: \n  90: ## Class context (as of 2026-04-20)\n  91: \n  92: - Two sections: **Period A** and **Period F**.\n  93: - **Week of 2026-04-27 schedule** (saved in project memory): Mon A 65 / Tue F 65 + A 55 / Wed A 65 + F **45** / Thu F 65 + A 55 / Fri F 65.\n  94: - **Period A** is one period behind Period F at start of 3-5 close-out. Both finish Topic 3 Thu 4/30. Period F starts 4-1 on Fri 5/1; Period A starts 4-1 on Mon 5/4.\n  95: - **Wednesday F = 45 min** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d short variant with Explore cut.\n  96: - **Solo teacher, class \u00e2\u2030\u00a410.** No aide-based release valves. Single-teacher circulation (4\u00e2\u20ac\u201c6 laps during Explore).\n  97: - **ELL-heavy** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d sentence frames on student packet are non-negotiable.\n  98: \n  99: ## Assessment coverage\n 100: \n 101: - **Topic 3 assessment (Thu 4/30)** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `a2topic3assess.docx`. 11 Qs spanning 3-1 through 3-5. Of these, 4 are Lesson 3-5 content: Q#2 (conjugate pairs \u00e2\u20ac\u201d preped via Tue\u00e2\u2020\u2019Wed bridge prompt), Q#5 (zeros + end behavior), Q#6 (Lucy's tray volume model \u00e2\u20ac\u201d paralleled by Storage Box #27 on Wed), Q#10 (identify zeros).\n 102: - **Topic 4 LEHS 8-Q assessment** \u00e2\u20ac\u201d `a2topic4assess.docx`, 8 selected items: #2, #3, #4, #5, #6, #7, #15, #19. Of these, 2 are Lesson 4-1 content: Q#3 (H/V asymptotes, from Ex 4/5), Q#5 (translation description, from Ex 5). **Practice #19 is the rehearsal item** for these.\n 103: \n 104: ## Related wiki pages (obsidian-wiki, home laptop)\n 105: \n 106: - `concepts/Klimsara-Adapted Lesson Pattern.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d 3-period template, phase timings, TPS rule, Wed-F variant\n 107: - `concepts/Single-DOK3 Lesson Spine.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d updated: per-period, not per-lesson\n 108: - `concepts/Self-Contained Pacer Pattern.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d v3 tabbed pattern\n 109: - `concepts/Do Now A-B-C Framework.md` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the school's Do Now sub-phasing convention\n 110: \n 111: ---\n 112: \n 113: <!-- gitnexus:start -->\n 114: # GitNexus \u00e2\u20ac\u201d Code Intelligence\n 115: \n 116: This project is indexed by GitNexus as **Lesson_planning** (29 symbols, 71 relationships, 6 execution flows). Use the GitNexus MCP tools to understand code, assess impact, and navigate safely.\n 117: \n 118: > If any GitNexus tool warns the index is stale, run `npx gitnexus analyze` in terminal first.\n 119: \n 120: ## Always Do\n 121: \n 122: - **MUST run impact analysis before editing any symbol.** Before modifying a function, class, or method, run `gitnexus_impact({target: \"symbolName\", direction: \"upstream\"})` and report the blast radius (direct callers, affected processes, risk level) to the user.\n 123: - **MUST run `gitnexus_detect_changes()` before committing** to verify your changes only affect expected symbols and execution flows.\n 124: - **MUST warn the user** if impact analysis returns HIGH or CRITICAL risk before proceeding with edits.\n 125: - When exploring unfamiliar code, use `gitnexus_query({query: \"concept\"})` to find execution flows instead of grepping. It returns process-grouped results ranked by relevance.\n 126: - When you need full context on a specific symbol \u00e2\u20ac\u201d callers, callees, which execution flows it participates in \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use `gitnexus_context({name: \"symbolName\"})`.\n 127: \n 128: ## When Debugging\n 129: \n 130: 1. `gitnexus_query({query: \"<error or symptom>\"})` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d find execution flows related to the issue\n 131: 2. `gitnexus_context({name: \"<suspect function>\"})` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d see all callers, callees, and process participation\n 132: 3. `READ gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/process/{processName}` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d trace the full execution flow step by step\n 133: 4. For regressions: `gitnexus_detect_changes({scope: \"compare\", base_ref: \"main\"})` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d see what your branch changed\n 134: \n 135: ## When Refactoring\n 136: \n 137: - **Renaming**: MUST use `gitnexus_rename({symbol_name: \"old\", new_name: \"new\", dry_run: true})` first. Review the preview \u00e2\u20ac\u201d graph edits are safe, text_search edits need manual review. Then run with `dry_run: false`.\n 138: - **Extracting/Splitting**: MUST run `gitnexus_context({name: \"target\"})` to see all incoming/outgoing refs, then `gitnexus_impact({target: \"target\", direction: \"upstream\"})` to find all external callers before moving code.\n 139: - After any refactor: run `gitnexus_detect_changes({scope: \"all\"})` to verify only expected files changed.\n 140: \n 141: ## Never Do\n 142: \n 143: - NEVER edit a function, class, or method without first running `gitnexus_impact` on it.\n 144: - NEVER ignore HIGH or CRITICAL risk warnings from impact analysis.\n 145: - NEVER rename symbols with find-and-replace \u00e2\u20ac\u201d use `gitnexus_rename` which understands the call graph.\n 146: - NEVER commit changes without running `gitnexus_detect_changes()` to check affected scope.\n 147: \n 148: ## Tools Quick Reference\n 149: \n 150: | Tool | When to use | Command |\n 151: |------|-------------|---------|\n 152: | `query` | Find code by concept | `gitnexus_query({query: \"auth validation\"})` |\n 153: | `context` | 360-degree view of one symbol | `gitnexus_context({name: \"validateUser\"})` |\n 154: | `impact` | Blast radius before editing | `gitnexus_impact({target: \"X\", direction: \"upstream\"})` |\n 155: | `detect_changes` | Pre-commit scope check | `gitnexus_detect_changes({scope: \"staged\"})` |\n 156: | `rename` | Safe multi-file rename | `gitnexus_rename({symbol_name: \"old\", new_name: \"new\", dry_run: true})` |\n 157: | `cypher` | Custom graph queries | `gitnexus_cypher({query: \"MATCH ...\"})` |\n 158: \n 159: ## Impact Risk Levels\n 160: \n 161: | Depth | Meaning | Action |\n 162: |-------|---------|--------|\n 163: | d=1 | WILL BREAK \u00e2\u20ac\u201d direct callers/importers | MUST update these |\n 164: | d=2 | LIKELY AFFECTED \u00e2\u20ac\u201d indirect deps | Should test |\n 165: | d=3 | MAY NEED TESTING \u00e2\u20ac\u201d transitive | Test if critical path |\n 166: \n 167: ## Resources\n 168: \n 169: | Resource | Use for |\n 170: |----------|---------|\n 171: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/context` | Codebase overview, check index freshness |\n 172: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/clusters` | All functional areas |\n 173: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/processes` | All execution flows |\n 174: | `gitnexus://repo/Lesson_planning/process/{name}` | Step-by-step execution trace |\n 175: \n 176: ## Self-Check Before Finishing\n 177: \n 178: Before completing any code modification task, verify:\n 179: 1. `gitnexus_impact` was run for all modified symbols\n 180: 2. No HIGH/CRITICAL risk warnings were ignored\n 181: 3. `gitnexus_detect_changes()` confirms changes match expected scope\n 182: 4. All d=1 (WILL BREAK) dependents were updated\n 183: \n 184: ## Keeping the Index Fresh\n 185: \n 186: After committing code changes, the GitNexus index becomes stale. Re-run analyze to update it:\n 187: \n 188: ```bash\n 189: npx gitnexus analyze\n 190: ```\n 191: \n 192: If the index previously included embeddings, preserve them by adding `--embeddings`:\n 193: \n 194: ```bash\n 195: npx gitnexus analyze --embeddings\n 196: ```\n 197: \n 198: To check whether embeddings exist, inspect `.gitnexus/meta.json` \u00e2\u20ac\u201d the `stats.embeddings` field shows the count (0 means no embeddings). **Running analyze without `--embeddings` will delete any previously generated embeddings.**\n 199: \n 200: > Claude Code users: A PostToolUse hook handles this automatically after `git commit` and `git merge`.\n 201: \n 202: ## CLI\n 203: \n 204: | Task | Read this skill file |\n 205: |------|---------------------|\n 206: | Understand architecture / \"How does X work?\" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-exploring/SKILL.md` |\n 207: | Blast radius / \"What breaks if I change X?\" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-impact-analysis/SKILL.md` |\n 208: | Trace bugs / \"Why is X failing?\" | `.claude/skills/gitnexus/gitnexus-debugging/SKILL.md` |\n 209: | Rename / extract / split / refactor | `.claude/skills/