9 329.63 cycles/sec \\u00e2\\u2020\\u2019 k = 26 \\u00c3\\u2014 329.63 = 8,570.38.\\\",\\n                    \\\"     New length 13 inches \\u00e2\\u2020\\u2019 f = 8,570.38 / 13 = 659.26 cycles/sec.\\\",\\n                ],\\n                color_hex=\\\"D9EAD3\\\")\\n\\n    add_callout(doc, \\\"\\u00e2\\u0161\\u00a0\\u00ef\\u00b8\\u008f  DIRECT vs INVERSE (both appear in today's DOK-3!)\\\",\\n                [\\n                    \\\"DIRECT: y = kx \\u00e2\\u2020\\u2019 y/x is constant. As x increases, y INCREASES proportionally.\\\",\\n                    \\\"INVERSE: y = k/x (xy = k). As x increases, y DECREASES proportionally.\\\",\\n                    \\\"Test: compute y/x (direct) AND xy (inverse). Whichever is constant tells you the relationship.\\\",\\n                ],\\n                color_hex=\\\"F4CCCC\\\")\\n    doc.add_paragraph()\\n\\n    ps.teal_section(doc, \\\"EXPLORE \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d Think-Pair-Share (33 min)\\\",\\n                    [\\\"Work with a partner. Move in order. Practice #26 (Ram\\u00c3\\u00b3n) is the big one \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d plan ~15 min for it.\\\"])\\n\\n    items = qb.get_for_packet(EXPLORE_IDS)\\n    labels = [\\n        \\\"Try It 3 \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d Ice cube melting\\\",\\n        \\\"Practice #12 \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d HOT: inverse SQUARE variation\\\",\\n        \\\"Practice #17 \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d Radio wavelength (graph)\\\",\\n        \\\"Practice #23 \\u00e2\\u20ac\\u201d Boyle's Law (volleyball vs basketball)\\\",\\n        \\\"Practice #26  \\u00e2\\u00ad\\u0090 PERFORMANCE TASK \\u00c2\\u00b7 Ram\\u00c3\\u00b3n's road trip\\\",\\n    ]\\n    for label, q in zip(labels, items):\\n        bank_item_block(doc, q, label=label, space_after_inches=1.5)\\n\\n    ps.teal_section(doc, \\\"SHARE / SUMMARY (5 min)\\\", [])\\n    ps.sentence_frame_box(doc, [\\n        \\\"Pair share (Ram\\u00c3\\u00b3n task): \\\\u201cPart A is ___ variation because distance and time have a constant RATIO of ___. Part B